From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:48:56 +0300
Subject: nouveau_mm: return NULL when no slab can be allocated

mm_slab_new() failing (out of GART) left the bucket empty and the allocator dereferenced it.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_mm.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_mm.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_mm.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_mm.c
@@ -194,8 +194,12 @@ nouveau_mm_allocate(struct nouveau_mman *cache,
    if (!list_is_empty(&bucket->used)) {
       slab = list_entry(bucket->used.next, struct mm_slab, head);
    } else {
-      if (list_is_empty(&bucket->free)) {
-         mm_slab_new(cache, bucket, MAX2(mm_get_order(size), MM_MIN_ORDER));
+      if (list_is_empty(&bucket->free) &&
+          mm_slab_new(cache, bucket, MAX2(mm_get_order(size), MM_MIN_ORDER))) {
+         /* out of memory: no slab to take a chunk from (the caller sees *bo unset) */
+         simple_mtx_unlock(&bucket->lock);
+         FREE(alloc);
+         return NULL;
       }
       slab = list_entry(bucket->free.next, struct mm_slab, head);
 
